  "releaseNotes": "Release candidate. Search results can rank differently from RC140926 — the fixes below correct\n      scores that were wrong, so rankings move for the better. Indexes are built from your documents on\n      load, so nothing stored needs converting; re-run `Index()` as usual.\n      \n      - Fixed: documents could all tie at the top score. Very common text fragments (the \"and\" in\n        ordinary prose) were weighted as if they were rare, and a long text field then pushed hundreds\n        of unrelated documents to the maximum score, burying the real match. Most visible with a long\n        searchable description field and with natural-language queries.\n      - Fixed: term frequency and length normalisation now count. Repeating a term in a document, a\n        shorter field, and `Field.BM25b` had almost no effect on BM25F scores; they now weigh as\n        documented. Same index size.\n      - Fixed: building a vector (embedding) index used memory growing with the fourth power of the\n        document count — 2.4 GB at 143 documents, out of memory on small servers. It now uses a fixed\n        12 MB cache plus the vectors (about 50 MB at 10 000 documents). Depends on HNSW 26.6.1848.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "IndxSearchLib",
  "verbatimVersion": "5.0.0-RC150926",
